//@version=6
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Multiday Anchored Auto VWAP by Bybllo
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// OVERVIEW
// This indicator plots up to 10 automatically anchored, rolling
// Volume Weighted Average Price (VWAP) lines - Rolling Day #0
// (today) through Rolling Day #9 (9 days ago) - plus 5 fully
// independent manual VWAP lines you anchor to any date/time you
// choose. Each line accumulates price*volume continuously from its
// own anchor point up to the current bar, giving a set of rolling,
// multi-day reference levels rather than a single VWAP that resets
// every day.
//
// INTENDED USE - FUTURES SCALPING / LOWER TIMEFRAMES
// This indicator is well suited to short-term futures scalping on
// instruments such as Nasdaq futures (NQ/MNQ). It's primarily used
// on the 1-minute chart, but the rolling VWAP levels hold up just as
// well on 2, 3, and 5-minute charts and other intraday timeframes -
// the anchor logic doesn't depend on your chart's timeframe at all,
// so the same 10 rolling-day levels stay valid however you're
// viewing the chart.
//
// AUTO MODE AND MANUAL MODE RUN TOGETHER, NOT AS A TOGGLE
// Unlike some anchored-VWAP tools that force you to choose between
// an automatic mode or a manual mode, the 10 automatic Rolling Day
// lines and the 5 Manual Input lines here are completely independent
// of each other and can be shown at the same time. You can, for
// example, keep the last 3 rolling days visible for a constantly
// up-to-date short-term picture while also anchoring a Manual Input
// line to a specific earnings date or session open that doesn't fall
// on a simple day count - both layers coexist without conflicting.
//
// WHY THE AUTO LINES NEVER GO STALE
// Every one of the 10 automatic Rolling Day anchor dates is
// recalculated from the live "now" (via timenow) every time the
// script runs, rather than being written as a fixed date in the
// code. This means there is no hardcoded date anywhere in the
// automatic section - the lines are always exactly "N days ago from
// today," permanently, with no need to ever edit or republish the
// script just because time has passed. The Manual Input lines work
// differently by necessity (Pine Script requires input() defaults to
// be fixed compile-time constants), so those 5 dates are hardcoded
// example values meant to be edited to whatever dates you actually
// want to anchor to.
//
// CALENDAR DAYS, NOT TRADING DAYS
// The 10 automatic lines count back in plain calendar days from
// today - weekends and holidays are not skipped or excluded. "3 days
// ago" always means exactly 3 x 24 hours back from the configured
// session start time, regardless of whether the market was open on
// that day. This is a deliberate design choice for simplicity and
// predictability; if you need trading-day-aware anchoring instead,
// see this author's companion script "Multiday VWAP by Bybllo."
//
// SESSION START TIME INPUT
// Instead of a full date/time picker for every automatic line, the
// auto section uses a single "Auto Mode Session Start Time (HHMM)"
// number field (default 1800 = 18:00, America/New_York time) that
// applies to all 10 rolling lines at once. Entering a value under
// 100 is automatically treated as an hour-only entry and expanded to
// HHMM format (e.g. entering 7 becomes 0700 / 07:00); entering a
// full 3-4 digit value like 715 sets both hour and minute (07:15).
// This lets you match the anchor time to your instrument's actual
// session open without touching 10 separate date pickers.
// The default of 18:00 (America/New_York) lines up directly with the
// Nasdaq futures (Globex) session open at 18:00 US Eastern Time.
// Because the calculation uses the named "America/New_York" timezone
// rather than a fixed UTC offset, Pine Script automatically applies
// the correct US Eastern Time / Eastern Daylight Time (EST/EDT) rule
// for whatever date is currently being evaluated - so this anchor
// stays aligned with the actual futures session open year-round, with
// no manual adjustment needed across the US daylight saving
// transition.
//
// ANCHOR START LABELS
// A single "Show Anchor Start Labels" toggle controls small
// speech-bubble labels (#0-#9 for the automatic lines, M1-M5 for the
// manual lines) at all 15 possible anchor points at once, each
// colored to exactly match its corresponding line. If a given line's
// own display toggle is off, its label is hidden too - you don't get
// orphaned labels for lines that aren't shown. These labels are kept
// out of the Style tab entirely and controlled only from the single
// Inputs-tab toggle, to keep the settings panel simple.
//
// CHART-TYPE COMPATIBILITY
// All price data is pulled via request.security() against the
// chart's own ticker rather than read directly off the chart, so the
// VWAP values are identical whether your chart is displaying
// candlesticks, Heikin Ashi, Renko, or any other non-standard chart
// type. Volume is unaffected by chart type and is used as-is.
//
// ANCHOR-POINT SAFETY GUARD
// Every VWAP calculation is guarded so that no price*volume
// accumulation happens before a line's actual anchor point - without
// this guard, anchored-VWAP calculations can show an artificial spike
// right at the anchor bar as leftover accumulated values get divided
// incorrectly. Each line here only starts accumulating exactly at
// its own anchor time, so the line begins cleanly with no distortion.
//
// HOW TO USE
// - Leave the automatic Rolling Day lines on for a quick, always-
//   current view of the last several sessions' VWAP levels. Adjust
//   "Auto Mode Session Start Time (HHMM)" if your market's session
//   doesn't start at 18:00 (America/New_York).
// - Enable any of the 5 Manual Input lines and pick an exact date/
//   time to anchor a VWAP to a specific event or session that
//   doesn't line up with a simple day count.
// - Turn on "Show Anchor Start Labels" to see a small badge at each
//   line's starting point on the chart.
// - Use the resulting lines as dynamic support/resistance or
//   fair-value reference levels, the same way a session VWAP is
//   used, but for whichever multi-day or custom-anchored period each
//   line represents.
// - Works well on Nasdaq futures 1-minute scalping charts, and holds
//   up just as well on 2/3/5-minute and other intraday timeframes.
//
// NOTES
// - The 10 automatic lines use plain calendar days (not trading
//   days), counted back from today - weekends are not skipped.
// - The default 18:00 (America/New_York) session start lines up
//   directly with the Nasdaq futures (Globex) session open. Since
//   the calculation uses the named "America/New_York" timezone,
//   Pine Script automatically applies the correct EST/EDT offset for
//   the current date, so this anchor stays aligned with the futures
//   session open year-round with no manual adjustment needed across
//   the US daylight saving transition.
// - Manual Input default dates are fixed values set at publish time
//   and will not update automatically; edit them periodically if you
//   want them to track recent dates.
// - This script requires volume data from your data provider. If no
//   volume is available for the symbol, the VWAP values will not
//   calculate correctly.
//
// DISCLAIMER
// For educational and informational purposes only. This is not
// financial advice. Past performance does not guarantee future
// results. Always verify how these levels behave on your specific
// symbol and timeframe before relying on them for live trading.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
indicator("Multiday Anchored Auto VWAP by Bybllo", overlay = true)
// ============================================
// INPUTS
// ============================================
// Auto mode session start time - no date, single field, entered as a
// number (HHMM). Default 1800 (=18:00, America/New_York). Entering a
// value under 100 (e.g. 7 or 07) is treated as an hour and
// auto-expanded to HHMM (7 -> 0700, i.e. 07:00. To set minutes too,
// e.g. 07:15, enter 715).
sessionTimeValue = input.int(1800, "Auto Mode Session Start Time (HHMM)", minval = 0, maxval = 2359, group = "Settings")
sessionTimeAdj = sessionTimeValue < 100 ? sessionTimeValue * 100 : sessionTimeValue
sessionHourFinal = int(sessionTimeAdj / 100)
sessionMinuteFinal = sessionTimeAdj % 100
show0 = input.bool(true, "Rolling Day #0 VWAP [Today]", group = "Auto - Display")
show1 = input.bool(true, "Rolling Day #1 VWAP [1 Day Ago]", group = "Auto - Display")
show2 = input.bool(true, "Rolling Day #2 VWAP [2 Days Ago]", group = "Auto - Display")
show3 = input.bool(true, "Rolling Day #3 VWAP [3 Days Ago]", group = "Auto - Display")
show4 = input.bool(true, "Rolling Day #4 VWAP [4 Days Ago]", group = "Auto - Display")
show5 = input.bool(true, "Rolling Day #5 VWAP [5 Days Ago]", group = "Auto - Display")
show6 = input.bool(true, "Rolling Day #6 VWAP [6 Days Ago]", group = "Auto - Display")
show7 = input.bool(true, "Rolling Day #7 VWAP [7 Days Ago]", group = "Auto - Display")
show8 = input.bool(true, "Rolling Day #8 VWAP [8 Days Ago]", group = "Auto - Display")
show9 = input.bool(true, "Rolling Day #9 VWAP [9 Days Ago]", group = "Auto - Display")
showLabels = input.bool(true, "Show Anchor Start Labels", group = "Display")
// ---- Manual Input #1-#5 (fully independent from Auto mode, 5 separate toggles) ----
// Defaults: today (2026-08-31) counting back one day at a time, 18:00 America/New_York
// (written as explicit -04:00 / EDT offsets here since input.time()
// requires a compile-time constant, which a named-timezone timestamp()
// call cannot provide - this only affects these fixed default values,
// not the auto rolling-day calculation below).
// These are fixed values - update periodically by editing the code.
showM1 = input.bool(false, "Manual Input #1", inline = "m1", group = "Manual Input")
mDate1 = input.time(timestamp('2026-08-31T18:00:00-04:00'), "", inline = "m1", group = "Manual Input")
showM2 = input.bool(false, "Manual Input #2", inline = "m2", group = "Manual Input")
mDate2 = input.time(timestamp('2026-08-30T18:00:00-04:00'), "", inline = "m2", group = "Manual Input")
showM3 = input.bool(false, "Manual Input #3", inline = "m3", group = "Manual Input")
mDate3 = input.time(timestamp('2026-08-29T18:00:00-04:00'), "", inline = "m3", group = "Manual Input")
showM4 = input.bool(false, "Manual Input #4", inline = "m4", group = "Manual Input")
mDate4 = input.time(timestamp('2026-08-28T18:00:00-04:00'), "", inline = "m4", group = "Manual Input")
showM5 = input.bool(false, "Manual Input #5", inline = "m5", group = "Manual Input")
mDate5 = input.time(timestamp('2026-08-27T18:00:00-04:00'), "", inline = "m5", group = "Manual Input")
// ============================================
// Force real market prices regardless of chart type (Heikin Ashi,
// Renko, etc.)
// ============================================
t = ticker.new(syminfo.prefix, syminfo.ticker)
[rh, rl, rc] = request.security(t, timeframe.period, [high, low, close])
realSrc = (rh + rl + rc) / 3
// ============================================
// Auto mode: recalculates "today" fresh every run and derives 0-9
// days ago from it. Session start time comes from sessionHourFinal /
// sessionMinuteFinal (default 18:00, America/New_York). No calendar
// UI here - the timenow-based approach means there is no hardcoded
// date, so it stays permanently up to date.
// ============================================
msPerDay = 86400000
todayY = year(timenow, 'America/New_York')
todayM = month(timenow, 'America/New_York')
todayD = dayofmonth(timenow, 'America/New_York')
startOfToday = timestamp('America/New_York', todayY, todayM, todayD, sessionHourFinal, sessionMinuteFinal, 0)
autoDate0 = startOfToday - 0 * msPerDay
autoDate1 = startOfToday - 1 * msPerDay
autoDate2 = startOfToday - 2 * msPerDay
autoDate3 = startOfToday - 3 * msPerDay
autoDate4 = startOfToday - 4 * msPerDay
autoDate5 = startOfToday - 5 * msPerDay
autoDate6 = startOfToday - 6 * msPerDay
autoDate7 = startOfToday - 7 * msPerDay
autoDate8 = startOfToday - 8 * msPerDay
autoDate9 = startOfToday - 9 * msPerDay
// ============================================
// Anchored VWAP accumulation
// ============================================
f_avwap(date) =>
    start = not na(date) and time >= date and time[1] < date
    sumSrc = realSrc * volume
    sumVol = volume
    sumSrc := start ? sumSrc : sumSrc + sumSrc[1]
    sumVol := start ? sumVol : sumVol + sumVol[1]
    sumSrc / sumVol
// ============================================
// PLOTS - Auto (guarded with time >= date so no accumulation happens
// before each line's anchor point, preventing a value spike)
// ============================================
plot(show0 and time >= autoDate0 ? f_avwap(autoDate0) : na, color = color.new(#ffe31b, 10),  title = "Rolling Day #0", linewidth = 1)
plot(show1 and time >= autoDate1 ? f_avwap(autoDate1) : na, color = color.new(#93af12, 10),  title = "Rolling Day #1", linewidth = 1)
plot(show2 and time >= autoDate2 ? f_avwap(autoDate2) : na, color = color.new(#f23645, 0),  title = "Rolling Day #2", linewidth = 1)
plot(show3 and time >= autoDate3 ? f_avwap(autoDate3) : na, color = color.new(#f57c00, 0),  title = "Rolling Day #3", linewidth = 1)
plot(show4 and time >= autoDate4 ? f_avwap(autoDate4) : na, color = color.new(#2962ff, 0),  title = "Rolling Day #4", linewidth = 1)
plot(show5 and time >= autoDate5 ? f_avwap(autoDate5) : na, color = color.new(#4caf50, 0),  title = "Rolling Day #5", linewidth = 1)
plot(show6 and time >= autoDate6 ? f_avwap(autoDate6) : na, color = color.new(#9c27b0, 0), title = "Rolling Day #6", linewidth = 1)
plot(show7 and time >= autoDate7 ? f_avwap(autoDate7) : na, color = color.new(#ffc107, 20), title = "Rolling Day #7", linewidth = 1)
plot(show8 and time >= autoDate8 ? f_avwap(autoDate8) : na, color = color.new(#067814, 20), title = "Rolling Day #8", linewidth = 1)
plot(show9 and time >= autoDate9 ? f_avwap(autoDate9) : na, color = color.new(#607d8b, 20), title = "Rolling Day #9", linewidth = 1)
// ============================================
// PLOTS - Manual Input #1-#5 (fully independent from Auto mode)
// Checkbox + color still appear normally in the Style tab (no
// editable restriction here).
// ============================================
plot(showM1 and not na(mDate1) and time >= mDate1 ? f_avwap(mDate1) : na, color = color.new(#f23645, 0),  title = "Manual Input #1", linewidth = 1)
plot(showM2 and not na(mDate2) and time >= mDate2 ? f_avwap(mDate2) : na, color = color.new(#f57c00, 0),  title = "Manual Input #2", linewidth = 1)
plot(showM3 and not na(mDate3) and time >= mDate3 ? f_avwap(mDate3) : na, color = color.new(#2962ff, 0),  title = "Manual Input #3", linewidth = 1)
plot(showM4 and not na(mDate4) and time >= mDate4 ? f_avwap(mDate4) : na, color = color.new(#4caf50, 0),  title = "Manual Input #4", linewidth = 1)
plot(showM5 and not na(mDate5) and time >= mDate5 ? f_avwap(mDate5) : na, color = color.new(#9c27b0, 0),  title = "Manual Input #5", linewidth = 1)
// ============================================
// Anchor start labels - a single "showLabels" toggle controls all 15
// possible labels at once. Each label's color exactly matches its
// corresponding line's color/opacity. If a given line's own display
// toggle is off, that line's label is hidden too. editable = false
// keeps these out of the Style tab entirely.
// ============================================
plotshape(showLabels and show0 and time >= autoDate0 and time[1] < autoDate0, text = "#0", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#ffe31b, 10), location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and show1 and time >= autoDate1 and time[1] < autoDate1, text = "#1", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#93af12, 10), location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and show2 and time >= autoDate2 and time[1] < autoDate2, text = "#2", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#f23645, 0),  location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and show3 and time >= autoDate3 and time[1] < autoDate3, text = "#3", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#f57c00, 0),  location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and show4 and time >= autoDate4 and time[1] < autoDate4, text = "#4", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#2962ff, 0),  location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and show5 and time >= autoDate5 and time[1] < autoDate5, text = "#5", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#4caf50, 0),  location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and show6 and time >= autoDate6 and time[1] < autoDate6, text = "#6", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#9c27b0, 0), location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and show7 and time >= autoDate7 and time[1] < autoDate7, text = "#7", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#ffc107, 50), location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and show8 and time >= autoDate8 and time[1] < autoDate8, text = "#8", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#067814, 40), location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and show9 and time >= autoDate9 and time[1] < autoDate9, text = "#9", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#607d8b, 30), location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and showM1 and not na(mDate1) and time >= mDate1 and time[1] < mDate1, text = "M1", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#f23645, 0),  location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and showM2 and not na(mDate2) and time >= mDate2 and time[1] < mDate2, text = "M2", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#f57c00, 0),  location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and showM3 and not na(mDate3) and time >= mDate3 and time[1] < mDate3, text = "M3", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#2962ff, 0),  location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and showM4 and not na(mDate4) and time >= mDate4 and time[1] < mDate4, text = "M4", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#4caf50, 0),  location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
plotshape(showLabels and showM5 and not na(mDate5) and time >= mDate5 and time[1] < mDate5, text = "M5", textcolor = color.white, color = color.new(#9c27b0, 0),  location = location.belowbar, style = shape.labelup, size = size.small, editable = false)
